WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.998
Electricity lights a lamp. It has
to flow all the way round a loop.

2
00:00:09.218 --> 00:00:13.444
That loop is a circuit. You can
build one, and make a lamp light.

3
00:00:13.944 --> 00:00:18.820
Electricity does jobs for us all
day. A lamp turns it into light.

4
00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:22.755
A kettle turns it into heat.
A cooker cooks our food.

5
00:00:22.975 --> 00:00:27.898
A fridge uses it to keep food
cold. A toy car uses it to move.

6
00:00:28.118 --> 00:00:32.901
A radio turns it into sound.
Electricity is not only for lights.

7
00:00:33.401 --> 00:00:37.441
The electricity in a wall socket
is strong. It can hurt you badly.

8
00:00:37.661 --> 00:00:41.330
Only a plug goes in a socket.
Never poke one with a pencil.

9
00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:45.451
Dry hands on switches. Water
lets electricity through to you.

10
00:00:45.671 --> 00:00:51.058
Never fly a kite near power lines.
If a wire is broken, tell a grown-up.

11
00:00:51.278 --> 00:00:55.132
A small cell is safe to hold.
Never put it in your mouth.

12
00:00:55.352 --> 00:00:59.068
Follow the rules when you build
a circuit, and you are safe.

13
00:00:59.568 --> 00:01:04.165
A simple circuit has three
parts: a cell, wires and a lamp.

14
00:01:04.385 --> 00:01:08.611
The cell is a small battery. It
pushes the electricity round.

15
00:01:08.831 --> 00:01:12.500
Add a wire, then the lamp.
The lamp is not lit yet.

16
00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:16.760
Add the second wire to close
the loop. Now the lamp lights!

17
00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:22.646
That loop is a circuit. Electricity flows
out of the cell, through the lamp, and back.

18
00:01:23.146 --> 00:01:27.186
Your circuit is a model of a
torch. Now take one wire out.

19
00:01:27.406 --> 00:01:30.936
The lamp goes out. There is
a gap, so the loop is broken.

20
00:01:31.156 --> 00:01:37.007
Electricity can only flow round a complete
loop. A gap anywhere, and it stops.

21
00:01:37.227 --> 00:01:41.685
Put the wire back. The loop is
complete, and the lamp lights again.

22
00:01:42.185 --> 00:01:46.783
Look inside a real torch: a battery,
two metal strips and a little lamp.

23
00:01:47.003 --> 00:01:51.740
A picture shows how the torch looks.
It does not show the loop inside.

24
00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:57.765
A diagram uses symbols. A long line
and a short line stand for the cell.

25
00:01:57.985 --> 00:02:01.932
A circle with a cross is the lamp.
Straight lines are the wires.

26
00:02:02.152 --> 00:02:06.564
The diagram is a model of the
torch. It shows the loop clearly.

27
00:02:07.064 --> 00:02:11.940
A torch has a switch. A switch
is a gap you can open and close.

28
00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:15.782
Switch it on, and the loop
closes. The lamp lights.

29
00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:19.578
Switch it off, and a gap
opens. The lamp goes out.

30
00:02:20.078 --> 00:02:24.862
Electricity does jobs for us all
day. Rules keep you safe with it.

31
00:02:25.082 --> 00:02:30.840
A cell, wires and a lamp in a complete
loop make a circuit. A gap stops it.

32
00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:36.494
A switch opens and closes a gap. A
diagram is a model of the circuit.
